00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.590
<b>#03
 Mima Takayuki</b>

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:18.380
Hello!

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:20.710
Hello!

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.590
I'm starving.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:23.640
What time is it?

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.380
It's 2:30.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.680
So grab a quick bite and then 
get ready for the meeting.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.830
I'll prepare the material.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.290
Yes, please do.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.980
<b>Stare</b>

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.980
<b>Stare</b>

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.320
Do I have something on me?

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:38.030
No, I just... noticed that 
sometimes you wear glasses,

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.710
and sometimes you wear contacts,

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:42.330
but I haven't been able to 
figure out the rule yet.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:44.410
Maybe it's that you wear contacts 
when you're trying hard?

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.810
His default is to wear contacts,

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.810
but if he didn't have enough time 
in the morning, he wears glasses.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.120
So if he comes in with glasses, 
just assume he overslept.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.910
Oh, you figured that out?

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.380
<i>That's such a banal reason...</i>

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.640
Yup, that's the reason for the glasses.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:03:59.030
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.380
<i>So is that what was happening 
in that briefing back there?</i>

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:04.960
<i>When he was rubbing his cheek or 
tucking his hair behind his ear...</i>

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.930
<b>Bam!</b>

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.260
<i>Those are all habits from 
pushing up your glasses!</i>

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:07.850
Miss

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.430
<i>I just realized that!</i>

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:12.110
Shake shake

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.680
What's wrong?

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.180
.It got him good

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.180
.It got him good

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.820
<i>I'm so sleepy.</i>

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:21.410
<b>Waver waver</b>

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:17.600
<i>Gonna go take a nap.</i>

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.110
Mima-san, perfect timing!

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.410
You're going to the nap room, aren't you?

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:25.200
So, this is the new eye mask 
from my friend's company.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.840
They're supposed to be really great!

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:30.130
I got a lot of samples, so please 
take one in your hour of need!

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.180
I'll use it. Thank you.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:34.700
Do you know how to use it?

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.400
...Yes.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.080
You really think I'm like 
some grandpa, don't you?

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.430
Of course not!

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.390
<b>Love   love</b>

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:42.710
You're more like a mascot!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.630
<b>Love   love</b>

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.680
<i>That's not any better...</i>

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.940
<i>So the meeting's in 40 minutes.</i>

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:51.110
<i>I'm going to sleep until the last minute.</i>

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.900
Mima, the meeting...

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.060
.Forgot to Pull It Down

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.060
.Forgot to Pull It Down

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.610
<b>Zzz   Zzz</b>

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:00.620
<i>Does he not know how to use eye masks?</i>

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:06.870
We need to take a hard look at our target market
 in order to increase our advertising reach.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.370
That's right.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:12.240
We might need a concrete strategy that 
effectively targets our younger user base.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.820
How's the workflow looking?

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.550
I can speak to that.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.330
This is last month's feedback.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.650
As you can see, our numbers 
are trending downward,

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:24.350
meaning that we don't have 
sufficient inbound traffic.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.460
About earlier...

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:32.120
Yes.

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:32.790
He took it off!

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.050
I feel like I need a brush up as well.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.050
I guess he noticed!

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:41.190
Mima!

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:42.110
Slap!

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:44.190
Let's go grab a drink!

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:44.190
Sparkle

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:47.670
<i>Ugh, I wanted to go home at a normal time.</i>

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.950
<b>Pub
Hakoneko</b>

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:51.350
Sorry for the wait. Here are 
the items your ordered.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:51.940
Thanks!

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:54.450
Good work. Tonight, we're gonna drink!

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.830
Good work.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.850
Nothing like a cold one 
after work, am I right?

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:03.890
You're really chugging them today.

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:04.630
Really?

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.960
How come you wanted to go 
drinking all of the sudden?

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:09.550
Huh?

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.520
I mean, you've been tired lately.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:14.480
Me?

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:18.000
<b>2nd beer</b>

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:16.890
Your face has no energy at all.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:18.250
And you screw up a lot.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.400
Both my face and screw ups are normal.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.940
I mean, I guess.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.420
But if I hadn't woken you up today,

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:26.510
you would've slept straight 
through the meeting.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.920
Excuse me, can I get another 
draft beer, please?

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:31.200
<i>Do I really look that tired?</i>

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.110
Another draft coming up!

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:33.960
<i>I kept wanting some kind of comfort,</i>

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:34.480
And a yakitori set, and a—

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.650
<i>but I didn't think it was 
because I was tired.</i>

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.980
W-Wait, one moment, please!

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:40.470
You know, though, if someone like 
me on the outside notices,

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:42.520
it means it's gotten quite bad already.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.250
If you properly looked inward,

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.360
you should be able to tell yourself to 
take it easier way before anyone else.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:51.030
The way I see it, you're bad 
at finding ways to unwind,

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:52.980
so you're missing out.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:54.720
<b>Slap slap</b>

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:57.120
I mean, just like with the hot drink!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.350
And the eye-mask!

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:01.190
Drunk\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:05.900
I say this because I worry about you.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.810
Another beer, please!

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.860
<i>I made him worry...</i>

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.050
Coming up!

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.770
<i>I guess that's my homework 
for the near future.</i>

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.460
Thank you so much for looking out for me.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.460
I will make sure to take 
better care of myself.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:20.910
<b>5th
beer</b>

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.730
Hey, why are you casually eating that?

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:27.630
<b>Chew chew</b>

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:21.670
<b>Sheesh</b>

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:23.690
That's <i>my</i> food!

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:25.700
Sorry.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:27.630
You don't look sorry at all!

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:29.530
Whatever, I'll drink more!

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.100
I think you've had enough.

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:34.430
It's fine. I'm paying, so go ahead.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:35.540
I'm full.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:37.640
There's some edamame left.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:38.550
Those are all empty pods.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.060
You're right.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:45.570
May I leave you and go home?

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:46.630
Nope.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:48.850
Let's go on another trip to 
find you something soothing.

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:49.740
No, thank you.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.780
Say what?

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.070
You gave me some good advice.

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:56.700
For the rest, I'll go figure it out myself.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.040
<b>Small Animals Cafe</b>

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.040
Comfort factor

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.510
<i>A small animals cafe?</i>

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.210
<i>Maybe this sort of thing 
is where I should start.</i>

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:08.350
<i>If nothing else, it looks more relaxing 
than going drinking with him.</i>

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.090
Should I get you home?

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.010
I can call a taxi.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:15.460
It's fine.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:17.910
They're nearby, so we'll 
 walk home together.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.300
Is this your girlfriend?

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.650
Naw. My little brother.

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:23.800
One of my comforts.

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:26.340
A comfort?

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.260
But I do think of you as 
a little brother, too.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.500
<i>I don't want a big brother like you.</i>

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:32.570
Carry me.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.220
No.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.040
Bro?

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:37.000
You got here fast!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.200
Sorry about that.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:40.640
I hope he didn't cause too much trouble.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:42.510
Thank you for taking care
 of my older brother.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:43.460
It wasn't—

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.410
Wrong, <i>I'm</i> taking care of <i>him</i>!

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.120
This is your brother's.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.870
Oh, thank you.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:51.780
Let's go home.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:52.760
Taxi?

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:53.730
Prolly...

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:55.650
Then let's walk over to the main street.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.050
<i>That's a good younger brother.</i>

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:01.000
Thank you!

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.020
Good job today, Mima!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.980
You, too.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.710
I feel sick.

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:07.710
There, there.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:12.640
<i>Just having a competent little 
brother could be a type of comfort.</i>

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:16.590
<i>I need to find my own brand of comfort.</i>

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:19.080
Souma...

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:19.740
Yeah?

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:22.600
The main street is in the 
total opposite direction...

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.080
Oh, well. Why not turn this into a walk?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.430
I'm seriously about to throw up...

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:04.930
<b>Coming up next</b>

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:04.930
<b>Shiki Souma</b>

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
